<title>UK: Shell Nigeria output now down 210,000 bpd - NNPC.</title>
<headline>Shell Nigeria output now down 210,000 bpd - NNPC.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal/Dutch Shell's Nigerian crude output is now running 210,000 barrels per day (bpd) below normal levels following community disturbances this week, an official with state Nigerian National Petroleum Corp (NNPC) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Earlier this week Shell's Forcados output, from the western region of the Niger delta, was reduced by 100,000 bpd from just under a million bpd.</p>
<p>The NNPC official said Bonny production, in the eastern delta region, had also now been hit.</p>
<p>OPEC member Nigeria pumps about two million bpd of crude, exporting around 1.7 million bpd.</p>
</text>
